  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing twenty-one songs over sixty-six minutes at Cat's Cradle in Carrboro, North Carolina, on January 27, 1999 [1]. It is the only available audio for this date and is rated five out of five by one listener [1]. The set includes early archive entries such as \"Letter From A Motel,\" \"You're In Maya,\" \"Commandante,\" \"Alpha Incipiens,\" and \"Born Ready\" [1]. Several tracks are rare, including \"Maize Stalk Drinking Blood,\" \"West Country Dream,\" and \"Yoga\" [1]. The performance also features the sole archived rendition of the Merle Haggard cover \"I Think I'll Just Stay Here And Drink\" [1]. A 2017 review of this specific recording by Shabby Veneer praises its brilliant sound quality and intimate atmosphere [2]. The reviewer highlights the amazing setlist from that period and a distinctive roughness in the vocalist's voice [2]. They describe it as a personal favorite and their most played live recording among their collection [2]. This show is the twenty-third of four hundred and sixty-seven archived performances for the band [3]. The previous archived show was at Rocket Bar on October 10, 1998 [3].",
